Z||000002||Robert||11-20-2000||07:13 PM||||If that’s the Mojave Desert in California I’m thinking of, I don’t think you would want to live (die) there in the summer.  It all to often gets in the 120’s.  We drove through there not long ago on a trip to Las Vegas. It was a mild 65 out, but you could tell by the plant life, it gets HOT there. <BR>Check out some of the photo’s I took, especially of my dream car.  See if you can figure out which car I lust after, (hint…. It’s black)   <BR>There’s even a shot for Moneyman fans.<P>Photo’s here  <A HREF="http://community.webshots.com/album/6712865MaTqbtTqEh" TARGET=_blank>http://community.webshots.com/album/6712865MaTqbtTqEh</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> “If you don’t look for that parking space near the entrance, you’ll never get it”<p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||10
