Z||000008||Robert||11-22-2000||08:42 PM||||Cheever2:<BR>Everything and more you wanted to know about the picture:<P>I took that picture in a museum in Boron, the only place left in the world that still mines for Borax, the stuff the helps us in so many ways (according to the video we watched) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Learn more about borax here: <A HREF="http://www.borax.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.borax.com/</A>    Way back before there were Fieros around, they used to transport the stuff out of the desert by 20 mule team, which is what the picture is depicting.<P>Here is a link about the town of Boron:  <A HREF="http://www.aeve.com/digitaldesert/boron/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aeve.com/digitaldesert/boron/</A> <BR>Just so you all can get a feel of what kind of life there is in the desert.<P>Hey Monkeyman, glad you liked the picture, WHEN are you going to return my 22P manual?<P>Later<P>Robert<BR>||||reg||10
